TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"transient","diagnosis":"Terminated the spec-build-driver worker session before it produced any file, envelope, or commit, so the ownership gate conflict-domains failed on a pristine lane rather than on any defect in the task's work. Evidence for a session/machinery fault rather than a worker fault: the recorded adapter error is result-projection-timeout — the configured finalMessage capture for adapter spec-build-driver was not projected within 10000 ms with exitEvidencePassed false — meaning no worker envelope of any kind (completion, needs-authority, or impossible) ever reached the driver, and the gate's own stderr 'agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base' is the downstream consequence. Independent inspection of the assigned worktree confirms the lane is untouched at the prepared base 71f2beb: `git status --porcelain` is empty, `git status --porcelain --ignored` is empty (no untracked or ignored residue), the stash is empty, the reflog's only entries are the preparation 'reset: moving to HEAD', and every path in the tree carries the identical worktree-creation mtime of 12:35:48. scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh were never created and results/receipts/proxy.json is absent, so the diff is empty with head == baseRev. This is specifically NOT the uncommitted-work trap that overseer steering comment 7 anticipated: that failure mode leaves modified or untracked files behind in the lane, and none exist here. Consequently there is no actionable in-domain fix to convert into attempt-2 steering, which rules out retry; and there is no missing authority, dependency, gate-contract defect, or out-of-task source fix — the declared conflict domains scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, tests are sufficient for the stated goal (the receipt path results/receipts/proxy.json sits under an already-tracked results/receipts directory) — which rules out blocked. The correct disposition is a machinery retry of the same attempt so the driver actually obtains a live worker session; the two attempt slots should not be spent on a session that never ran. The existing authorized steering remains valid and sufficient for the re-run: apply --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 for text-only serving instead of the superseded VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY steer, keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6, reuse the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding rather than inventing generators, and commit only in-domain paths before exiting with a clean `git status --porcelain`. One factual correction for whoever re-runs: /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy does not exist on the host filesystem at diagnosis time, so the 'do not rebuild what exists' steering holds only if the checkpoint is present inside the container; otherwise make-proxy.sh must build it."}
